# 211-APP-0045 — The shell's window opens only when the user asks — done

**Type:** tools (`shell`) · **Owner:** tools track (`APP`) · **Priority:** P1 (the maintainer's report from the MacBook Pro, 2026-10-10) · **Status:** done (2026-10-10) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** [211](../issues/211-intel-pc-from-a-sata-ssd.md) · **Roadmap:** track G · **Constitution:** MC-11.5

Numbered from the kernel track's request in `requests-APP.md` ("The shell's window opens only when the user asks", 2026-10-10), at the maintainer's report from the MacBook Pro (`fast-test` a00618b): "a program started by itself when `wm` started (the shell). It should not start by itself, only at the user's request from `wm`'s menu."

## Problem

[211-APP-0040](211-APP-0040-the-shells-commands-in-console.done) opens the shell's window whenever the shell starts a window manager, so it appears at every start of `wm`, unasked. The local gate found the same: the `windows` suite's test manager `winmgr` got the shell's window as a third window.

## Plan

- The shell opens its window only when asked: Ctrl+Alt+F5 (the shell takes the key whatever program has the keyboard). Starting a window manager opens nothing.
- `wm`'s menu item `shell` asks the shell for its window through `SLOT_SHELL`: that is [211-APP-0044](../issues/211-APP-0044-console-joined-to-the-shell.md), waiting for 211-KRN-0058. Until then the menu has no such item.
- The shell's help and `docs/tools` (EN, RU) say so.

## Acceptance criteria

- **The `wm` suite:** `wm` starts with its three programs' windows and no shell window; Ctrl+Alt+F5 opens it; closed with Alt+W, it goes and `wm` keeps running; Ctrl+Alt+F5 opens it again.
- The `windows` suite passes again (`winmgr` finds the two test windows alone).
- On the MacBook Pro, `wm` starts with the desktop and its programs alone.

## Related

[211-APP-0040](211-APP-0040-the-shells-commands-in-console.done), [211-APP-0044](../issues/211-APP-0044-console-joined-to-the-shell.md).

## Resolution

- `shell/src/main.rs`: the shell no longer opens its window when it starts a window manager; Ctrl+Alt+F5 opens it, whatever program has the keyboard. The shell's and `console`'s help and `docs/tools` (EN, RU) say so.
- **The `wm` suite (x86, on the branch, 2026-10-10):** `wm fm, clock, top` starts with the three programs' windows and no shell window (no `[SHELL] THE SHELL'S WINDOW OPENED` either); Ctrl+Alt+F5 opens it for the shell's checks (`ps`, `date`, `logs`, `top` in a window, resize, `reboot`'s question, `fg` refused); closed with Alt+W it goes and `wm` goes on in its normal mode; Ctrl+Alt+F5 opens it again; it opens once more for `camera` in the shell's window. The rest of the suite is as before 211-APP-0040 (three windows). The `windows` suite passes again (`winmgr` finds its two test windows alone), and so does the `tablet` suite, back to its form before 211-APP-0040.
- **Left:** the item in `wm`'s right-click menu (the maintainer, 2026-10-10) needs the channel to the shell: [211-APP-0044](../issues/211-APP-0044-console-joined-to-the-shell.md), raised to P1, waiting for 211-KRN-0058 (`SLOT_SHELL`) in `main`. The maintainer's check on the MacBook Pro: `fast-test` from b0d00e3.
